{
  "Motif": "vampires",
  "Name": "Vampires",
  "Draw": "Vampires are aristocratic undead in human shape: tall, thin, very still, with bloodless white skin pulled tight over the bone, dark eyes set deep, long nails and visible teeth. Their clothing is fine and decades out of date, and worn perfectly - high collars, brocade, lace, long coats, mourning dress. The lesser ones are further gone and further down: hunched, ragged, more animal than noble. The only red in the picture is where blood actually is.",
  "ElementDraw": {
    "fire": "The clothing smoulders at the hems and the skin has cracked and gone black at every exposed edge, as though the light has already found it. Hot orange from below.",
    "ice": "Frost on the collar and the lashes, the skin gone blue-white and glassy. Everything around it fogs and it has no breath of its own.",
    "lightning": "Arcs run the rings, the buttons and the fine chain at the throat, the hair lifts, and the eyes are lit yellow from inside.",
    "earth": "Grave soil still on the clothing and roots grown through the coat. The skin is dried dark and drawn like something dug up, in green-black.",
    "arcane": "Violet light behind the eyes and under the skin picking out the veins, the edges of the figure smearing, and nothing of it reflecting in anything."
  },
  "ValidFloors": [
    4,
    8
  ],
